<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Winchester</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Venta Belgarum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Winchester is a cathedral city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hampshire">Hampshire</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venta-belgarum">Venta Belgarum</a> it was the Roman capital of the Belgae, and it later became the chief royal seat of the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-the-great">Alfred the Great</a>, and an early capital of England. Its cathedral, begun in 1079, is one of the largest in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/winchester.jpg" alt="Winchester" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: (CC BY-SA 2.0) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Winchester_Montage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
